{"slug":"longest-common-prefix","title":"Longest Common Prefix","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"easy","order":119,"tags":["strings","prefix"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Shrink the candidate","body":["The common prefix of a list of words can only be as long as the shortest agreement. Start with the first word as the candidate and compare it with each other word, cutting the candidate down to the part both share.",{"code":"prefix = words[0]\nfor w in words[1:]:\n    k = 0\n    while k < len(prefix) and k < len(w) and prefix[k] == w[k]:\n        k += 1\n    prefix = prefix[:k]"},"The candidate never grows, so after the last word it is the longest prefix that all words share. It may become empty."]},"statement":["You are given `k` words. Print the longest string that is a prefix of every word. If the words have no common prefix, print -1."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `k`.","Each of the next `k` lines has one word."],"outputFormat":["Print the prefix, or -1 if it is empty."],"constraints":["1 <= k <= 100","1 <= length of each word <= 200","The words contain lowercase letters."],"examples":[{"input":"3\nflower\nflow\nflight\n","output":"fl\n","note":"All three start with fl."},{"input":"2\ndog\ncar\n","output":"-1\n","note":"Nothing in common."}],"hints":["Start with the first word as the candidate prefix.","For each other word, find how many leading letters it shares with the candidate.","Cut the candidate to that length. If it becomes empty, the answer is -1."],"starter":{"python":"k = int(input())\nw = [input().strip() for _ in range(k)]\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long k;\n    cin >> k;\n    vector<string> w(k);\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        cin >> w[i];\n    }\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long k = sc.nextLong();\n        String[] w = new String[(int) k];\n        for (int i = 0; i < w.length; i++) {\n            w[i] = sc.next();\n        }\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Keep the first word as the candidate and shorten it to the part shared with each following word."],"complexity":"Time O(total number of letters), space O(1) besides the input.","code":{"python":"k = int(input())\nw = [input().strip() for _ in range(k)]\n\nprefix = w[0]\nfor word in w[1:]:\n    j = 0\n    while j < len(prefix) and j < len(word) and prefix[j] == word[j]:\n        j += 1\n    prefix = prefix[:j]\nprint(prefix if prefix else -1)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long k;\n    cin >> k;\n    vector<string> w(k);\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        cin >> w[i];\n    }\n\n    string prefix = w[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        size_t j = 0;\n        while (j < prefix.size() && j < w[i].size() && prefix[j] == w[i][j]) j++;\n        prefix = prefix.substr(0, j);\n    }\n    if (prefix.empty()) cout << -1 << \"\\n\";\n    else cout << prefix << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long k = sc.nextLong();\n        String[] w = new String[(int) k];\n        for (int i = 0; i < w.length; i++) {\n            w[i] = sc.next();\n        }\n\n        String prefix = w[0];\n        for (int i = 1; i < w.length; i++) {\n            int j = 0;\n            while (j < prefix.length() && j < w[i].length() && prefix.charAt(j) == w[i].charAt(j)) j++;\n            prefix = prefix.substring(0, j);\n        }\n        System.out.println(prefix.isEmpty() ? \"-1\" : prefix);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"3\nflower\nflow\nflight\n","output":"fl\n"},{"input":"2\ndog\ncar\n","output":"-1\n"},{"input":"1\nalone\n","output":"alone\n"},{"input":"2\nsame\nsame\n","output":"same\n"},{"input":"2\nab\nabc\n","output":"ab\n"},{"input":"3\nabc\nab\na\n","output":"a\n"},{"input":"6\nxyzxyzcacbccb\nxyzxyzbabba\nxyzxyzcccac\nxyzxyza\nxyzxyzc\nxyzxyzbcacb\n","output":"xyzxyz\n"},{"input":"10\nacbacb\nbbcbbacb\nbaccc\nccbcca\ncaba\nab\nabccab\na\nc\naac\n","output":"-1\n"},{"input":"100\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaccbaaa\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaabcac\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaabaca\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaacb\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaacababcc\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaabbcbba\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaacbaca\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaabacccc\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa